      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the stuffing paste: blend parsley, half the garlic, a little chilli, and salt into a rough paste. Make small cuts in the fish and push the paste into the cuts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a large stockpot over high heat. Fry the fish for 3 minutes per side until golden. Remove."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the same pot, fry the diced onion for 5 minutes. Add tomato puree and cook for 5 minutes, stirring."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the blended onion, tinned tomatoes, remaining garlic, and chilli. Cook over high heat for 20 minutes until thick and the oil separates."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the stock. Nestle in the carrots, sweet potato, and cabbage. Return the fish on top. Simmer for 20 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the fish and vegetables carefully. Set aside. You now have about 900ml of flavoured broth in the pot."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the washed rice to the broth. Stir, bring to the boil, then reduce to very low heat. Cover tightly and cook for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and broth absorbed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Arrange rice on a large platter. Place fish and vegetables on top. Serve with chilli sauce on the side."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Fish falls apart when removed from the pot",
              "cause": "Fish overcooked in the initial frying or simmered too long",
              "fix": "Fry fish quickly just to seal it, then remove from the broth while still slightly firm"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Rice is stodgy and the sauce has not absorbed",
              "cause": "Too much liquid left in the pot when rice was added",
              "fix": "Allow some evaporation before adding rice, aiming for about 1.5 times the volume of rice in liquid"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Sauce tastes very acidic from the tomatoes",
              "cause": "Tomato base not cooked down long enough",
              "fix": "Cook the tomato base until it looks dark red and the oil has fully separated before adding stock"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thieboudienne is the national dish of Senegal and one of the most important dishes in West African cooking. Its name in Wolof means rice and fish. The dish was created in the 19th century in Saint-Louis, Senegal's historic northern city. In 2021 it was added to the UNESCO list of Intangible Cultural Heritage. It is eaten at the midday meal in most Senegalese homes and is considered the measure of a cook's ability."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
